+   * ever flush that DPB, so a slot can hold one picture for the whole life of a room — and a frame
+   * that predicts from it with a null residual (or re-displays it outright) decodes to that
+   * picture, PRISTINE, carrying a brand-new timestamp.
+   *
+   * That is the artefact a spectator probe caught 9 times across two Stuntman runs on 2026-08-08:
+   * single frames of 4.2 s / 6.0 s / 20.2 s / 35.1 s / 53.6 s-old content spliced between two
+   * correct consecutive frames, with the sender's RTP clock provably monotonic ([ts-mono]
+   * violations=0 / 13376 samples) and 8 of the 9 landing when NO peer was dropping any layer.
+   *
+   * Strict layering fixes both halves at once:
+   *   maxNumRefFramesInDPB = numTemporalLayers  — one slot per layer, nothing left over to go stale
+   *   numFwdRefs = 1                            — a frame predicts from ONE picture, the most
+   *                                               recent in a layer <= its own
+   *   enableLTR = 0, ltrNumFrames = 0           — no long-term slot survives the ladder's rotation
+   * so the oldest picture anything can reference is the previous base-layer frame (<= 2 frames back
+   * at 3 layers). Dropping an upper layer is then reference-safe BY CONSTRUCTION — nothing below it
+   * could have referenced it — and a stale-reference re-emission, if one still happened, would
